GIMP LiquidRescale Plug-In
=====================

Copyright (C) 2007-2010 Carlo Baldassi <carlobaldassi@gmail.com>
(implementation based on the GIMP Plug-in Template by Michael Natterer)

This package is a plug-in for GIMP 3.0 or newer (this branch; GIMP 2
needs the releases before the port). It is a frontend to
the LiquidRescale Library (liblqr) which implements the algorithm
described in the paper "Seam Carving for Content-Aware Image Resizing"
by Shai Avidan and Ariel Shamir, which can be found at
https://faculty.idc.ac.il/arik/SCWeb/imret/imret.pdf

Building and installing (GIMP 3)
--------------------------------

The build uses meson. liblqr is taken from the system if it has it
(pkg-config lqr-1), otherwise it is downloaded and built into the
plug-in (-Dbundled_liblqr=enabled forces that):

    meson setup build -Dgimp_plugindir=$HOME/.config/GIMP/3.2/plug-ins/gimp-lqr-plugin
    ninja -C build install

(3.2 is the profile folder of GIMP 3.2; GIMP 3.0 uses 3.0.)

Without -Dgimp_plugindir the plug-in goes to the plug-in folder of the
GIMP installation that pkg-config finds. The translations and the manual
are installed next to the plug-in (locale/ and help/). The plug-in is
Layer > Liquid rescale..., and plug-in-lqr in the procedure browser.
The INSTALL file is the generic text of autotools, which this branch no
longer uses.

For the Flatpak GIMP, gimp-plugin-devtools/gimp-build.sh (from
github.com/sandbranch/gimp-plugin-devtools, next to this folder) runs the
same commands inside the GNOME SDK that GIMP was built with.

Tests
-----

    tests/run.sh          # or tests/run.sh --asan

builds the plug-in into tests/output and tests it in the Flatpak GIMP
without a window, with a throwaway GIMP profile in tests/output: your
own profile and plug-ins are not touched. It prints PASS or FAIL for each
case and exits non-zero on any failure. tests/gui/ opens the dialog on a
Broadway display, to look at it; it is not part of the automatic tests.

Happy GIMPing,
--Carlo
